--Description: Thinking process ► We need the 21-and-older population for every Dubuque-County ZIP code that recorded Bourbon sales in 2022 (those seen earlier: 52001, 52002, 52003, 52040, 52068, 52033).  
--1) The census table lists population counts by gender and age bands; adults are rows where minimum_age ≥ 21.  
--2) Summing both “male” and “female” rows gives the total adult population; NULL/blank gender rows are skipped so we don’t double-count.  
--3) Aggregate by zipcode to return one row per ZIP, ready to join with sales data later.
SELECT
  zipcode,
  SUM(population) AS pop_21_plus
FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_usa.population_by_zip_2010`
WHERE minimum_age >= 21
  AND LOWER(gender) IN ('male', 'female')
  AND zipcode IN ('52001','52002','52003','52040','52068','52033')
GROUP BY zipcode
ORDER BY zipcode;
